_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-29T06:08:12Z","updated_at":"2025-11-29T10:28:22Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.5.stable\nGodot 4.5.1.stable\nGodot 4.6..dev4.official\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Windows 10 (build 19041) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8157) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 15.93 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using enums in GDScript, the documentation on hover does not work properly for individual enum values. Instead of showing the constant's description, it shows \"No description available\" instead.\n\nHovering over a variable of type `EnumTest` works fine (shows enum and its values' docstrings):\n<img width=\"907\" height=\"581\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9f70e9db-ba0a-4cba-89c3-94620cf19a81\" />\n\nHovering over the type `EnumTest` directly works fine (shows enum's docstring):\n<img width=\"917\" height=\"530\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/63425346-a28e-4b51-893d-6b621573de29\" />\n\nHovering over a constant/value from `EnumTest` does **not** work (shows \"No description available instead\"):\n<img width=\"897\" height=\"538\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/217ec569-d16d-45d5-b784-e200ea607c66\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create an enum\n- Add documentation to the enum and its values (either inline or multiline before value)\n- Add a statement that explicitly uses one of the constants defined in the enum\n  - Example: `if test == EnumTest.ONE`\n- Hover over the constant\n- Instead of the proper documentation, \"No description available\" is shown\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[enum_docstring_bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23831972/enum_docstring_bug.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113305/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":3},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113305/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}